# Root build context only — Docker applies this file to builds whose context is
# the repo root. The compose file builds from ./backend and ./web, so each of
# those directories needs its OWN .dockerignore (M1 deliverable — see
# docs/roadmap.md, Milestone 1). This root file still matters for any
# `docker build .` run and for keeping private/ and .env out of every context.
private/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
data/
audio/
